1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,948
You have three maps, some things, and two people.

2
00:00:03,848 --> 00:00:07,529
What you don't have yet is a story that ties them together.

3
00:00:09,329 --> 00:00:11,261
Today Pim wants her tablet back,

4
00:00:11,711 --> 00:00:13,528
the pump wants three fuses,

5
00:00:13,978 --> 00:00:17,685
and one bad idea with a crowbar loses the whole game.

6
00:00:18,585 --> 00:00:20,781
Every bit of it is an answer in a room.

7
00:00:21,981 --> 00:00:25,840
A choice has a condition in front of it, and outcomes behind.

8
00:00:26,740 --> 00:00:28,801
You've used both since the third lecture.

9
00:00:30,601 --> 00:00:33,258
On a map there are two new conditions.

10
00:00:34,158 --> 00:00:37,138
Holding asks what the person answering is carrying.

11
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:40,928
Party asks what everybody on the ground is carrying between them.

12
00:00:42,728 --> 00:00:44,086
And there are new outcomes.

13
00:00:44,986 --> 00:00:47,679
Give and take move things in and out of a pack.

14
00:00:48,579 --> 00:00:50,986
Open and reveal work on props.

15
00:00:51,886 --> 00:00:55,537
Calm, rouse, dismiss and summon work on people.

16
00:00:56,737 --> 00:00:58,199
First a quest that waits.

17
00:00:59,099 --> 00:01:01,389
Here it is in the Quest Log,

18
00:01:01,839 --> 00:01:05,338
on the ePADD of a crew member who beamed back up.

19
00:01:06,238 --> 00:01:09,627
Pim's Tablet, a hundred credits, and two paragraphs.

20
00:01:11,427 --> 00:01:13,810
In the file, it starts when it's revealed,

21
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,056
which means when an answer says so.

22
00:01:16,956 --> 00:01:20,063
The second paragraph is about who Pim is,

23
00:01:20,513 --> 00:01:23,183
for whoever stayed on the ship and never met her.

24
00:01:24,083 --> 00:01:26,564
Lint warns that nothing reveals it yet,

25
00:01:27,014 --> 00:01:28,251
and that's true for now.

26
00:01:30,051 --> 00:01:31,998
Then two things that begin hidden.

27
00:01:32,898 --> 00:01:35,927
Here's the yard on the engineer's map, near the end,

28
00:01:36,377 --> 00:01:38,608
and that's Pim, standing by the tent.

29
00:01:39,508 --> 00:01:41,952
In the file she's a second record.

30
00:01:42,402 --> 00:01:45,986
When somebody goes somewhere else on a map, they're two records:

31
00:01:46,436 --> 00:01:48,729
the one who leaves, and the one who arrives.

32
00:01:50,529 --> 00:01:52,973
And here's the gully on his map,

33
00:01:53,423 --> 00:01:56,436
with a medical kit by the rock that wasn't there before.

34
00:01:57,336 --> 00:01:59,082
In the file it's a prop,

35
00:01:59,532 --> 00:02:01,718
hidden until a scene shows it.

36
00:02:02,918 --> 00:02:04,262
Now for her scene,

37
00:02:04,712 --> 00:02:07,555
and it's where most of today's words live.

38
00:02:09,355 --> 00:02:11,862
This is the Act app on the engineer's handheld,

39
00:02:12,312 --> 00:02:14,595
talking to Pim in the gully.

40
00:02:15,495 --> 00:02:17,856
He's read the notice by the pump house,

41
00:02:18,306 --> 00:02:21,515
so he's offered a question about the spare cell.

42
00:02:23,315 --> 00:02:27,406
In the file, that answer is only offered if the party learned a fact,

43
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:29,298
from the notice by the door.

44
00:02:30,198 --> 00:02:31,737
This one reveals the stash.

45
00:02:32,637 --> 00:02:35,904
In the next room, a promise accepts the quest.

46
00:02:37,704 --> 00:02:39,740
And here's the payoff, on the handheld.

47
00:02:40,190 --> 00:02:41,759
He's carrying the tablet now,

48
00:02:42,209 --> 00:02:43,924
and there are two new buttons.

49
00:02:45,724 --> 00:02:49,813
In the file, the first is offered only to the one holding the tablet.

50
00:02:50,713 --> 00:02:53,692
Then three outcomes in a row, with commas:

51
00:02:54,142 --> 00:02:57,746
take the tablet, complete the quest, and give a fuse.

52
00:02:59,546 --> 00:03:01,304
The second is the mean answer.

53
00:03:01,754 --> 00:03:03,727
Keep the tablet, and she's roused:

54
00:03:04,177 --> 00:03:07,162
she attacks, and the quest fails.

55
00:03:08,062 --> 00:03:09,263
And when she goes home,

56
00:03:09,713 --> 00:03:11,827
one answer dismisses her here

57
00:03:12,277 --> 00:03:14,671
and summons her there.

58
00:03:15,871 --> 00:03:17,752
The pump needs three fuses now.

59
00:03:18,652 --> 00:03:20,756
Here's the panel on the engineer's handheld,

60
00:03:21,206 --> 00:03:22,940
with two fuses in his pack.

61
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:27,847
He's offered the wire and the crowbar, and not the lever.

62
00:03:29,647 --> 00:03:32,150
With a third fuse the line changes,

63
00:03:32,600 --> 00:03:35,141
and fitting all three is the first button.

64
00:03:36,941 --> 00:03:39,381
In the file, look at the condition,

65
00:03:39,831 --> 00:03:42,023
and at the outcome after it.

66
00:03:42,923 --> 00:03:45,140
Holding three, and take three.

67
00:03:46,940 --> 00:03:49,891
Take always takes from the person who answers.

68
00:03:50,341 --> 00:03:54,424
So the condition in front of it is always holding, and never party.

69
00:03:56,224 --> 00:03:58,161
The lines at the top are different.

70
00:03:58,611 --> 00:04:00,978
A line is read by everybody,

71
00:04:01,428 --> 00:04:03,669
so a line asks about the party.

72
00:04:05,469 --> 00:04:07,381
The second answer is a gamble.

73
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:09,532
Two fuses and a bit of wire,

74
00:04:09,982 --> 00:04:11,646
and a roll that can fail.

75
00:04:12,546 --> 00:04:14,213
And notice where the signal went.

76
00:04:14,663 --> 00:04:16,868
Two answers lead to this room now,

77
00:04:17,318 --> 00:04:19,642
so the signal sits on its one way out.

78
00:04:20,842 --> 00:04:23,489
The starter's terminal already teaches a fact.

79
00:04:23,939 --> 00:04:25,124
Give it a second use.

80
00:04:26,024 --> 00:04:29,285
On the handheld, once the code is copied down,

81
00:04:29,735 --> 00:04:32,460
there's a new button under Send the door code.

82
00:04:34,260 --> 00:04:38,032
In the file, send the sentry its update, and it's calm.

83
00:04:38,482 --> 00:04:40,321
It keeps its power cell, though,

84
00:04:40,771 --> 00:04:42,388
so the party still needs another one.

85
00:04:44,188 --> 00:04:46,510
And Marrow gets one answer about the brass key.

86
00:04:47,410 --> 00:04:50,210
Here it is on the weapons officer's handheld,

87
00:04:50,660 --> 00:04:53,034
and it's the engineer who's carrying the key.

88
00:04:53,934 --> 00:04:57,027
In the file, that condition is party,

89
00:04:57,477 --> 00:04:58,903
because nothing is taken,

90
00:04:59,354 --> 00:05:01,654
and it doesn't matter who picked the key up.

91
00:05:02,854 --> 00:05:06,844
You wrote no Win line today, and no Lose line.

92
00:05:07,744 --> 00:05:08,868
You didn't need to.

93
00:05:09,318 --> 00:05:11,663
Both sit on the starter's quest.

94
00:05:13,463 --> 00:05:15,595
Here's the last screen after the crowbar,

95
00:05:16,045 --> 00:05:18,191
and that's the starter's Lose sentence.

96
00:05:19,091 --> 00:05:21,179
Your crowbar fails that quest,

97
00:05:21,629 --> 00:05:24,411
so it loses the game from two maps away.

98
00:05:26,211 --> 00:05:29,942
And here's the beacon, with the spare cell in the engineer's pack.

99
00:05:30,842 --> 00:05:32,828
Your spare is a power cell,

100
00:05:33,278 --> 00:05:36,960
so the starter's own winning answer takes it,

101
00:05:37,410 --> 00:05:40,415
and the game ends with the starter's Win sentence.

102
00:05:42,215 --> 00:05:43,970
One more word, discover,

103
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:46,730
tells the ship an area exists.

104
00:05:47,630 --> 00:05:49,120
It isn't in your mission,

105
00:05:49,570 --> 00:05:53,116
because the ship can't beam into your cistern anyway.

106
00:05:54,316 --> 00:05:55,684
Play the long way round.

107
00:05:56,584 --> 00:05:59,017
First the weapons officer puts the sentry down,

108
00:05:59,467 --> 00:06:01,057
with one full shot.

109
00:06:01,957 --> 00:06:03,723
Shots miss a lot,

110
00:06:04,173 --> 00:06:06,988
and no app tells you a shot hit or missed.

111
00:06:08,788 --> 00:06:10,984
The key, then Marrow, and then the gully.

112
00:06:11,884 --> 00:06:13,266
Pim asks for her tablet.

113
00:06:14,166 --> 00:06:16,407
The engineer puts the crawler down,

114
00:06:16,857 --> 00:06:19,657
with a full shot from the foot of the stairs.

115
00:06:20,557 --> 00:06:23,547
Then the tablet, and back to Pim for a fuse.

116
00:06:24,447 --> 00:06:26,304
Three fuses in the pump,

117
00:06:26,754 --> 00:06:29,343
then the gate, and the spare cell.

118
00:06:30,243 --> 00:06:32,626
Pim opens the relay house from across the yard,

119
00:06:33,076 --> 00:06:34,449
and the beacon lights.

120
00:06:36,249 --> 00:06:38,797
Then play it again, and lose it with the crowbar.

121
00:06:40,597 --> 00:06:44,060
For the exercise, give Marrow a use for the medical kit,

122
00:06:44,510 --> 00:06:47,468
and write a second losing answer that plays fair.

123
00:06:49,268 --> 00:06:51,471
That's the last new word for a while.

124
00:06:51,921 --> 00:06:54,700
Next time, the screen your crew has been looking at.
